{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:9dd19974c3adea5f","name":"WED Treadwell","source":{"id":"source:reference-9dd19974c3adea5f","title":"WED Treadwell","revision":24712,"timestamp":"2024-11-05T20:17:56Z","sha256":"fe01eab3b60c7eacad95bbcaf4c1a8fe5729389d9d8eef1143a1751403e408f9","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=24712","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=WED%20Treadwell&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-9dd19974c3adea5f","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Books: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rebellion Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rebellion_Era_Campaign_Guide"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Web Enhancements"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Web_Enhancements"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Star Wars Miniatures Previews"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Star_Wars_Miniatures_Previews"},")"]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The WED Treadwell is not the most famous or most successful Repair Droid, but a large number of them have been manufactured and sold throughout the galaxy. Because the Droid has a simple appearance (that of a rolling platform with a viewer on a stalk and four or more tool arms) raiders and pirates often overlook it when plundering. As a result, the Treadwell is one of the least often stolen Droids. In fact, Treadwells are sometimes mistaken for tool racks, which is unsurprising since they act as rolling tool racks for their owners. Treadwells are not particularly bright and don't have much drive, but these factors make them obedient and reliable, and they are especially popular on fringe worlds where residents are suspicious of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Although WED Treadwells are fragile, requiring regular maintenance and environments that contain few hazards, they have a reputation for being adaptable and alert. The arms of a Treadwell can be swapped out quickly and easily, and many owners keep a stockpile of specialty arms for specific jobs. The Droids are also simple-minded, doing whatever they are told until they complete the task or receive new instructions. \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["WED Treadwells can be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["WED Treadwell Statistics (CL 0)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Small ",{"tag":"a","children":["2nd-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/2nd-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 2\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +4; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +6\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenceId":"reference:ee1c8277caf5fb9b"},", 1 Unassigned\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 14 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 11), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 8, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},": 10\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org